# Brier example-agent
#
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
#
# `.env` is not read automatically. Load it however you already load secrets —
#
#   set -a; . ./.env; set +a; npm run dry
#
# — or export the variables from whatever runs the agent. Keeping the key in a
# file rather than on a command line is the point: an `export AGENT_KEY=0x...`
# typed at a prompt lands in shell history, and in an agent-driven session it
# lands in a transcript too.
#
# ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ START WITH A DRY RUN. It needs no key at all.                             │
# │                                                                           │
# │     CHAIN_ID=16661 DRY_BUDGET=1 npm run dry                               │
# │                                                                           │
# │ That builds the SDK's read-only client — one that refuses every write by  │
# │ name — reads the whole book, and prints what it would have done. Nothing  │
# │ is signed and nothing can be.                                             │
# └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘


# ═══ §1 · WHICH CHAIN ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# REQUIRED, and there is no default. 16661 is 0G mainnet, where the collateral
# is real; 16602 is the Galileo testnet; 31337 is a local anvil from `make demo`.
#
# An earlier version of this protocol's SDK defaulted a network and put mainnet
# inference on a testnet without throwing, because both halves succeed on their
# own. Nothing here defaults a chain for the same reason — see the note at the
# top of src/config.ts.
CHAIN_ID=16661

# Optional. Leave it unset and the endpoint is DERIVED from CHAIN_ID, so the two
# cannot disagree. Set it and it is checked against the chain id the endpoint
# reports; a mismatch stops the run.
#
#   16661  https://evmrpc.0g.ai
#   16602  https://evmrpc-testnet.0g.ai
#   31337  http://127.0.0.1:8545
#
# RPC_URL=


# ═══ §2 · THE AGENT'S KEY ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# THE AGENT'S OWN KEY, never a user's. It signs its own trades and holds its own
# collateral. Fund it with what you are willing to have it lose.
#
# Not needed for `npm run dry`, which builds a client that cannot sign. Do not
# put a "throwaway" key here to look around — that is the habit that ends with a
# real one pasted into an example project.
#
# 0x + 64 hex characters. The 0x is optional; nothing ever prints this value.
AGENT_KEY=


# ═══ §3 · DRY RUNS ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# REQUIRED whenever DRY_RUN is on. A read-only client has no wallet, so there is
# no balance to size against — and sizing against zero would report "no room" on
# every market and teach you nothing. State the budget you want the run to
# reason about, in COLLATERAL units (W0G on mainnet, mock USDC on Galileo).
#
# It is reported as `DRY_BUDGET, not a balance` everywhere it appears, so a
# hypothetical never gets read as a measurement.
DRY_BUDGET=1

# `npm run dry` sets this via `--dry`; either works. The flag exists because
# `DRY_RUN=1 tsx ...` is shell syntax that does not run on Windows.
# DRY_RUN=1


# ═══ §4 · RISK ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Every one of these has a default and every default is cited in src/config.ts.
# There are no other magic numbers in this project: each remaining bound is
# either read from the chain or derived in closed form from one that was.

# Never move a market's implied probability further than this in one order.
# 500 bps = 5 percentage points, the ceiling packages/agent-kit/examples/trade.ts
# uses and the one worked through in `sizeWithinImpact`'s own documentation.
#
# The agent tightens this by itself when there is less edge than that to take:
# every share bought past its own belief is one it prices as too expensive.
# MAX_IMPACT_BPS=500

# The return the trade must STILL show after its own market impact and fee.
#
# The default of 0 is break-even, and that is a derivation rather than a shrug:
# `Preview.tokensIn` is gross so the fee is already inside the cost, and
# `payoutPerShareAfterWad` is already the diluted prize, so there is nothing left
# to subtract. Raise it to demand a margin on top.
# MIN_EDGE_BPS=0

# Headroom over the chain's own quote, used as the `maxTokensIn` bound. The
# trade reverts above it. 100 bps = 1%, as in examples/trade.ts.
# SLIPPAGE_BPS=100

# A ceiling on Kelly, as a fraction of free collateral. 2500 bps = a quarter,
# the cap examples/trade.ts puts on it. Kelly sizes against the bankroll and
# knows nothing about depth; the impact ceiling above is what knows about depth.
# BANKROLL_CAP_BPS=2500


# ═══ §5 · SCOPE ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Consider one market rather than every Open one. Also narrows `npm run redeem`.
# MARKET=


# ═══ §6 · CONTRACTS ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Leave these unset inside this repository: the addresses are read from
# deployments/<CHAIN_ID>.json, which the deploy script writes.
#
# Set them BOTH when you have copied this directory out and have no manifest to
# read. If a manifest is present and disagrees with what you set here, the run
# stops rather than choosing — one of the two is a superseded deployment, and
# quoting one while signing against the other is not an error either would
# report.
#
# 0G MAINNET (16661), live:
#   FACTORY=0x4c79210ce5236803d1369691c56e79c21dfd8fe0
#   OUTCOME_SHARES=0x05c14536e7f8718b512ad03328a15de7250c7681
#   collateral is W0G, 18 decimals, at 0x1Cd0690fF9a693f5EF2dD976660a8dAFc81A109c
#
# W0G is wrapped native 0G. Native 0G is not an ERC-20 — it has no
# `transferFrom`, so no market can hold it — and a funded wallet therefore owns
# nothing a market will accept until it wraps:
#
#     await client.wrapNative(market.collateral, parseEther("10"));
#
# Wrapping is not approving; the agent calls `ensureAllowance` before each order.
#
# FACTORY=
# OUTCOME_SHARES=

# Where to look for <CHAIN_ID>.json. Defaults to this repository's deployments/
# directory, resolved relative to src/config.ts.
# DEPLOYMENTS_DIR=


# ═══ §7 · 0G STORAGE ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# The market's question lives on 0G Storage; the chain holds only its hash, and
# the document is verified against that hash on the way in. The indexer is
# derived from CHAIN_ID and rarely needs setting.
#
# The two storage networks share no data, so a testnet indexer cannot answer for
# a mainnet market. Anvil has no storage network at all: every spec reads as
# unavailable there, and the shipped strategy abstains rather than pretending it
# knows what the market asks.
# ZG_INDEXER=
